"question-b1d2632a-4694-5c22-b050-b15669bba222"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186087786 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-58130b5b-5f37-553e-8991-9f3dd2a84005" "question-5bcab4b1-53e9-547b-81a4-3bf0881c104a" "question-3d2f4bec-f2bc-5622-80f4-e5a5ebaa94bf"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-41e7831f-c290-5b73-a0b9-fe7067c749d0" :question/id #uuid "41e7831f-c290-5b73-a0b9-fe7067c749d0" :question/math-academy-id "q-15857" :question/problem "![](images/33/33070b4b871552c4c45f21f0885cbce45ff65eb278cb000e68c91adfc2ab004c.png)\n\nConsider the circle of radius $16$ centered at the origin, as shown above. Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ),$  traverse the circle once in the counterclockwise direction starting at the point $A(16,0)?$" :question/worked-solution "The parametric equations of a circle  of radius $r$ centered at  the origin are\n\n$$\nx=r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$\n\nUnder this parametrization, the circle is traversed once in the counterclockwise direction, starting from $(r,0).$\n\nIn our case, the radius $r=16.$ Therefore, the parametric equations of the circle are \n\n$$\nx=16\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=16\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dd164691-a7a0-5f7f-b4dc-78db7c18f818"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dd164691-a7a0-5f7f-b4dc-78db7c18f818" :answer-field/id #uuid "dd164691-a7a0-5f7f-b4dc-78db7c18f818" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-c2332f56-6db7-5b68-8801-e4c7db637aba" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c2332f56-6db7-5b68-8801-e4c7db637aba" "answer-c7b32d97-9055-5b1f-81e6-1ec5f053894d" "answer-31a45883-2a84-5b7d-9f25-dbf675d5147b" "answer-47bf6ae0-f1fd-5c54-9d5a-c1dcfb3a7